More debug logging (no behavior change) for the same investigation:
requires patches/preemption-offload-debug-logging.patch and
patches/preemption-defer-block-free.patch applied first.

The fix in preemption-defer-block-free.patch is confirmed working as
designed (live trace: 2 in-flight offload store jobs correctly flushed
and waited for, ~1s) but did NOT resolve the actual symptom -- a
preempted-mid-prefill request still recomputes from scratch on retry
(0% cached tokens, same TTFT as before the fix). Since only 2 jobs were
ever in-flight (the vast majority of the request's ~50 chunks had
already completed their store long before preemption), the real cause
must be upstream of block-free timing entirely.

This adds one targeted logger.debug() call right after the scheduler
computes num_computed_tokens (local + external) for a request's lookup,
scoped to request.num_preemptions > 0 (i.e. only retries, so it's cheap
and low-volume) -- logs the local hit, external hit, total hit, and
critically hit_diverged/load_kv_async, since hit_diverged is literally
the "local hit's resume boundary has no valid Mamba state, reconcile to
a boundary every group agrees on" signal from
kv_cache_manager.get_computed_blocks_for_connector() -- exactly the
kind of thing that could explain a total (not partial) cache miss on a
retry despite the underlying block data being intact.

--- a/v1/core/sched/scheduler.py
+++ b/v1/core/sched/scheduler.py
@@ -829,6 +829,21 @@
                     num_computed_tokens = (
                         num_new_local_computed_tokens + num_external_computed_tokens
                     )
+                    if request.num_preemptions > 0:
+                        logger.debug(
+                            "request-logging preemption-debug: lookup result for "
+                            "retried req %s (attempt #%d): num_prompt_tokens=%d "
+                            "local_hit=%d external_hit=%d total_hit=%d "
+                            "hit_diverged=%s load_kv_async=%s",
+                            request.request_id,
+                            request.num_preemptions,
+                            request.num_prompt_tokens,
+                            num_new_local_computed_tokens,
+                            num_external_computed_tokens,
+                            num_computed_tokens,
+                            hit_diverged,
+                            load_kv_async,
+                        )
                     assert num_computed_tokens <= request.num_tokens
 
                     # Skip request with pending mm encoding prefetches
